-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/26623c18-8abc-5738-af3d-6d1dc6b68d5f
-- title:
--   Generic fibre of blow-up chart C[J/varpiₜ] is formally smooth
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** A prime $q$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (hypothesis `hqM'`), and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). A field $L$ of characteristic $0$, an element $\zeta \in L$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ`), and the hypothesis `hι` that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$.
--
--   **Level and function field.** A subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ which by `hH₁` equals the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ (available because $\ell \mid M' \mid q^2M'$); so $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. An intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ which by `hK` is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ generated over $L$ by the image, under the coefficientwise embedding [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the field of $q$-expansions of the rational modular functions for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   **Base ring.** A discrete valuation domain $A$ which is an $L$-algebra with $L$ as its fraction field, is Henselian local and has algebraically closed residue field; $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAq`); $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \subseteq K$. An element $j \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$ (`hj`), and $j \neq 0$. A uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$ (`hϖ`: the maximal ideal is $(\varpi)$), and an element $\varpi_t$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   **Chart algebra and supersingular point.** Throughout, $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A ↥K j` is $j$ regarded as an element of $C$. A maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), such that (`hss`) for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of elements $j_0$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no non-zero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **Point of the integral model.** A point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the two chart algebras), together with the element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ obtained by pulling $\varpi$ back along the structure morphism `toBase` to a global section and taking its germ at $z$ (`hϖz`), assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`); a point $y'$ of `XFin A ↥K j` $= \mathrm{Spec}\,C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` (`hy'`), satisfying the same supersingularity condition as above with $y$ replaced by $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ (`hss'`), and `hy'y` asserting $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$.
--
--   **Drinfeld chart witness.** A discrete valuation domain $W_1$, complete for its maximal-adic topology, with a ring homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ such that the maximal ideal of $W_1$ is generated by $\sigma_1(\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`); power series $f_1, u_1, v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 \equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $= X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`); and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e_1 : \widehat{\mathcal{O}_{X,z}} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v_1 - f_1u_1\big),$$
--   where $\widehat{\mathcal{O}_{X,z}}$ is the adic completion of the stalk with respect to its maximal ideal. Write $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mk}_S$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germ}_{y'} : C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ for the composite of the canonical identification of $C$ with the sections of $X$ over the image of `ιFin` with the germ map at $z$.
--
--   **The hypothesis `hW₁`** is a conjunction of seven clauses, concerning these data.
--
--   (1) *Constants*: for every $a \in A$, $e_1$ carries the image in $\widehat{\mathcal{O}_{X,z}}$ of the germ at $z$ of the global section attached to $a$ to $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1 a))$.
--
--   (2) *Stability of the chart*: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, $p_g$ having non-zero associated Laurent series, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the image under `coeffEmb L` of the quotient of the series of $p_f$ by that of $p_g$, and every $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, one has $\iota_*(\tau x) \cdot (g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})^\wedge = (f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})^\wedge$ as $q$-expansions, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\delta$ is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} \delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/q \\ q\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$ — the automorphism $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$.
--
--   (3) *Triviality on the residue field at $y'$*: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ as in (2) preserving $C$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ satisfies $\tau(a) - a \in y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ for all $a \in C$.
--
--   (4) *Linearisation of the action on the Drinfeld chart*: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and satisfying $\tau(a)-a \in y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ for all $a \in C$, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W_1$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W_1)$ such that: $\theta$ intertwines the map $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_{y'}$ with the action of $\tau$ on $C$; $\theta$ fixes every constant $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(w))$, $w \in W_1$; for each $j' \in \{0,1\}$, $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S(X_{j'})) - \mathrm{mk}_S(\sum_i C(M_{ij'})X_i)$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_0), \mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)$; $c^{q+1} - 1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_1$; $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W_1$ for all $i,j$; if $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$ then $c - 1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_1$; and if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$, then $c-1$ does not lie in the maximal ideal of $W_1$.
--
--   (5) *Separation of branches*: for all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and all prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ such that each $P_i$ omits at least one of $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_0), \mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)$, each contains $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$, and each contains an element $\mathrm{mk}_S\big(C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h\big)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC}$ to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ are distinct.
--
--   (6) *Valuation criterion along one branch*: for every prime $P$ of $S$ omitting at least one of $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_0), \mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)$, containing $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$ and containing some $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and every $a \in C$: $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_{y'}(a))$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image under $A \to L$ of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   (7) *Drinfeld witness for $j(\mathsf{q}^q)$*: there exist a proof that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) — the Laurent series obtained from the $j$-series by multiplying all exponents by $q$ — lies in $K$, a proof that the resulting element of $K$ lies in $C$, an element $a_0 \in A$ with that element minus the image of $a_0$ in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and a power series $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that: for all $a,b \in W_1$ not both in the maximal ideal of $W_1$ and with $a^qb - ab^q$ in the maximal ideal, the element $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^i b^{\,e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W_1$; and $e_1$ sends $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_{y'}(\cdot))$ of that element of $C$ minus the image of $a_0$ to $\mathrm{mk}_S(h)$.
--
--   **The centre and the blow-up chart.** An ideal $J$ of $C$ which by `hJ` is the infimum of the set of those ideals $J'$ of $C$ for which there exist $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of (2) and maps $C$ into $C$, with $J'$ the contraction along the induced endomorphism of $C$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_{y'}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t))$, $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_0)$ and $\mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)$. Finally an $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ which by `hB` is the $A$-subalgebra underlying the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ x\,\varpi_t = i\}$, that is the blow-up chart $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** The fibre of $B$ over the zero prime of $A$, namely `(⊥ : Ideal A).Fiber ↥B` $= \kappa(\bot) \otimes_A B$, is a formally smooth algebra over $\kappa(\bot) =$ `(⊥ : Ideal A).ResidueField`, the residue field of $A$ at $\bot$.
--
--   This is the generic-fibre step in the verification that the weighted blow-up chart $C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra, along the centre $J$ cut out by the Drinfeld local model at the supersingular point, gives a smooth model: over the fraction field of $A$ the blow-up changes nothing of substance, and smoothness follows from finite type, integral closedness and Krull dimension at most one over a perfect field. It feeds the combined smoothness statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.formallySmooth_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.formallySmooth_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_dvd), in the auxiliary-level frame in which the full level $\Gamma(q\ell)$ is replaced by a diamond condition modulo a guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$.
